From 4ef3f45b83574fa3451dd7db6ddd99e100cd9e5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:46:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the native Catalog screen to match the real website
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous patch made MainActivity's WebView wrapper the launcher
again after "convert the web into the app" was misread as "wrap the
site in a browser view." The very next message corrected that
directly: the app should not open as a webpage. This undoes that
revert and goes back to NativeActivity as the launcher/App Links
target, then actually redesigns its Catalog/home screen in Compose to
match public/index.html instead of leaving it as a bare search box and
list:

- Force the light theme in NativeActivity: the site has no dark mode,
  so the app shouldn't switch to the near-black Material scheme when
  the phone is in system dark mode (the cause of the "bare black
  screen" screenshot).
- CatalogViewModel: filter visibleCourses by selected category/stage in
  addition to search (mirrors app.js's renderCourses() predicate), plus
  a popularCourses list ranked by student count, unaffected by filters.
- New CategoryIcons.kt: the 8 fixed category pills and 5 education-
  stage options from app.js's hardcoded arrays, their icons, and the
  course-card icon badge mapping (iconFor() ported 1:1) — there is no
  thumbnail/cover image anywhere in the courses API, so this icon badge
  is the real "image" on both web and native.
- CourseCard: icon badge instead of initials-on-a-color-block, student
  count next to the rating, and an Add to cart/In cart button wired to
  the existing CartStore.
- New CatalogHomeSections.kt + restructured CatalogScreen: hero (copy,
  search, live stats) -> category pills -> stage strip -> featured
  course grid -> popular courses list -> promo cards (instructor /
  live classes, handed off to the website via Custom Tabs, same as
  checkout) -> benefits strip, in the same order as index.html.
- Bump versionCode/versionName for the next Play Console upload.

Scope: Catalog/home screen only. Course Detail, Checkout, My Learning,
Account and Login/Register keep their current plain Material3 look for
now, as a deliberate next step rather than an oversight.

